# Cybernetic — Business-Logic Modules: Design & Logic Report

> Scope: `backend/src/modules/business-logic-modules/`
> Companion infra: `backend/src/infra/application-db/schema/`, `backend/src/common/casl/`, `backend/src/utils/shared/`
> This is the canonical merged report. It folds in the `alignment_link` fix (formerly
> `structure-fix-version1`), adds a per-sub-module logic reference (§10), and a ranked
> issues/bugs register found during full analysis (§11).

---

## 1. The big picture — what this system *is*

Cybernetic is an **OKR + execution-tracking engine**. The 14 modules under
`business-logic-modules/` divide into four conceptual layers that build on each other:

```
┌─ IDENTITY / ORG STRUCTURE ─────────────────────────────┐
│  Organization → Department → Team → Person             │  WHO does the work
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
            │ owns / is scoped to
            ▼
┌─ OKR / STRATEGY ───────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Objective → KeyResult        Initiative               │  WHAT we aim for
│         └──── Alignment (graph links objectives) ──┘    │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
            │ initiatives are executed via
            ▼
┌─ EXECUTION ────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Task (sub-tasks, assignees) + Label                   │  HOW work gets done
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
            │ every state change flows through
            ▼
┌─ TELEMETRY / LEARNING ─────────────────────────────────┐
│  Tracking (event log + projections)  Intervention      │  WHAT actually happened
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

The unifying design thesis: **strategy (OKR) and execution (tasks) are separate
concerns wired together by an append-only event log.** The static modules describe
*intent*; the tracking module records *reality*; projections reconcile the two.

