## 8. How the modules combine — three end-to-end flows

**Flow A — Define strategy:**
`Objective` created (scoped to a team) → `KeyResult`s attached → `Alignment` links
ladder this objective up to a department/org objective → `OkrTreeService.buildTree`
renders the whole cascade with live progress %.

**Flow B — Execute and track:**
`Initiative` created and linked to KRs → `Task`s (with sub-tasks, assignees, labels)
created under it → user hits `POST /tracking/tasks/:slug/start` → `TrackingService`
appends a `started` event, projects it to `task_state` + `task.status` atomically →
`POST /tracking/tasks/:slug/time` accumulates `totalTimeLoggedMinutes` → timeline
endpoint replays the full event history.

**Flow C — Close the loop:**
A KR is lagging → `Intervention` created with a hypothesis, linked to that KR → over the
measurement window, `POST /tracking/key-results/:slug/measure` writes measurements →
`key_result.currentValue` updates → `OkrTreeService` recomputes progress → intervention
concluded against observed movement.

The connective tissue is consistent: **controllers resolve `slug`→entity under a tenancy
context, check coarse policy; services apply row-level CASL and business rules; repos do
tenant-scoped SQL; the tracking event log is the spine that records every transition
immutably.**

