## 10. Per-sub-module logic reference (what each module actually does)

> Columns: **Endpoints** = HTTP surface (controller); **Service logic** = business rules
> beyond passthrough; **Repo notes** = noteworthy SQL behavior; **Authz** = how it's
> gated. "Passthrough CRUD" = service forwards to repo with existence check only.

### organization
- **Endpoints:** create / update / delete / search / get by id|slug|name.
- **Service logic:** passthrough CRUD; `requireBy*` existence helpers.
- **Repo notes:** standard soft-delete CRUD; `findByName` for uniqueness lookups.
- **Authz:** coarse only (admin `manage`, others `read`). Acceptable (§3).

### department
- **Endpoints:** create / update / delete / search / roots / by-parent.
- **Service logic:** `findRoots` (parentId null) + `findByParentId` build the nested
  chart; otherwise passthrough.
- **Repo notes:** self-FK `parentId`. **No cycle guard on re-parenting** (§11 #7).
- **Authz:** coarse only.

### team
- **Endpoints:** create / update / delete / search / by-department.
- **Service logic:** passthrough; `findByDepartmentId` for org rollups.
- **Repo notes:** `departmentId` required but not existence-checked at write (§11 #5).
- **Authz:** coarse only.

### person
- **Endpoints:** create / update / delete / search / get by id|slug|name.
- **Service logic:** `update` is row-level authorized (`update Person`, members limited
  to `{ id: user.id }`); `remove` is **not** row-level authorized (§11 #8).
- **Repo notes:** **strips `passwordHash` from every read/returning** via
  `safePersonColumns` — credential never escapes. (Strength.)
- **Authz:** mixed (update row-level, remove coarse).

### objective
- **Endpoints:** create / update / delete / search / get by id|slug / by-owner / by-scope.
- **Service logic:** `update`/`remove` row-level authorized; `findByScope(scope,
  scopeRefId)` drives scoped rollups.
- **Repo notes:** polymorphic `scope`+`scopeRefId`; **`scopeRefId` not validated against
  `scope`** at create (§11 #5).
- **Authz:** row-level on mutate.

### key-result
- **Endpoints:** create / update / update-value / delete / get / search / by-objective.
- **Service logic:** `computeKrProgress` lives in `OkrTreeService`, not here; KR service
  itself is passthrough. `updateCurrentValue` is the tracking write seam.
- **Repo notes:** decimals as `decimal(20,4)` strings; `objectiveId` not existence-checked.
- **Authz:** **coarse only** — no `assertAbility` on any mutation (§11 #8). Safe because
  only managers/admins can write KRs, but asymmetric.

### initiative
- **Endpoints:** create / update / delete / search / queryAll / get / by-owner /
  link-KR / unlink-KR / list-KR-ids.
- **Service logic:** `update`/`remove` row-level authorized. Status is a denormalized
  cache; the authoritative value is `initiative_state`.
- **Repo notes:** `linkKeyResult` dedups in app code (racy, no DB unique — §11 #6); KR
  existence not checked (§11 #5).
- **Authz:** row-level on mutate.

### alignment (incl. okr-tree)
- **Endpoints:** `GET okr/tree/:objectiveSlug`, `POST alignment/link`, `POST alignment/unlink`.
- **Service logic:** `link` validates self-link, endpoint existence/liveness, and
  duplicates (added in the fix). `OkrTreeService.buildTree` recursively renders the graph
  with cycle guard; `computeKrProgress` is direction-aware with degenerate-case handling.
- **Repo notes:** `alignable_type` enum on `from_type`/`to_type`; partial unique index on
  the edge tuple; `findChildren`/`findParents` filter soft-deleted.
- **Authz:** coarse (`AlignmentLink`). No row-level (edges have no per-row owner).

### task (incl. task.util)
- **Endpoints:** create / search / summary / get by id|slug / update / delete /
  assignees add+remove / labels add+remove.
- **Service logic:** richest authorization surface — `requireBySlugForWrite`,
  `requireBySlugAuthorized`, `requireByIdAuthorized` separate read vs write row-level
  gates; `summary` → `countByInitiative` rollup. `buildTaskKey` renders `TASK-<seq>`.
- **Repo notes:** insert omits `sequenceId` (DB sequence assigns it); `update` strips
  `status`/`sequenceId`/identity fields; assignee/label links dedup in app (racy, §11 #6);
  `parentId`/`initiativeId`/`personId`/`labelId` not existence-checked (§11 #5);
  re-parenting has no cycle guard (§11 #7).
- **Authz:** row-level on direct edits — **but bypassed by the tracking lifecycle (§11 #1).**

### label
- **Endpoints:** create / update / delete / queryAll (+ get by id).
- **Service logic:** passthrough CRUD with existence check.
- **Repo notes:** self-FK `parentId` label hierarchy; no cycle guard.
- **Authz:** coarse only.

### tracking (incl. projection/*)
- **Endpoints (`/tracking`):** initiative lifecycle (start/pause/resume/block/unblock/
  complete/cancel), `time`, `reason`, `outcome`, `timeline`; task lifecycle (same set),
  `time`, `timeline`; `key-results/:slug/measure`.
- **Service logic:** `appendAndProject` (atomic append + dual projection),
  `measureKeyResult` (append + project + measurement row + currentValue), `emit`/
  `emitLifecycle` wrappers, post-commit `notify`.
- **Repo notes:** `activity_event` append-only; `listBySubject` returns the full ordered
  timeline (no actor filtering — §11 #2); projectors upsert state read-models.
- **Authz:** **coarse `create/read ActivityEvent` only — no row-level subject check
  (§11 #1/#2).**

### intervention
- **Endpoints:** create / update / delete / get / search / link-KR / unlink-KR / list-affected-KR.
- **Service logic:** `update`/`remove` row-level authorized; `findAffectedKeyResultIds`
  for future window-vs-measurement analysis.
- **Repo notes:** `linkKeyResult` dedups in app (racy, §11 #6); KR existence unchecked.
- **Authz:** row-level on mutate; `status` is free CRUD (no transition enforcement).

